# Quality auto-mark rule: any run of >=3 consecutive identical raw readings for the
# same IOA within one reporting window is marked QUALITY=SUSPECT by the historian's
# own duplicate-detection pass. This marker is computed here at the historian, not on
# the wire — it will NOT appear in the RTU's own QDS byte in iec104_capture.pcap.
# Normal RTU reporting interval: 10s. Live readings vary by +/-1.5A run to run.
# A SUSPECT run is a held/replayed historian cache record, not an RTU observation: its
# displayed value can be stale even though the RTU stream remains good. This breaker log's
# stored engineering range is 150.0A through 550.0A; held records differ from live input
# by more than 5.0A before the console marks them for operator review.
#
